# Git LFS is deliberately NOT used in this repository.
#
# It used to track *.zip / *.gz / *.tar and friends for the ~862 MB dataset
# corpus under datasets/. That corpus blew the account's GitHub LFS budget, and
# because a clone has to smudge LFS pointers to check out the working tree, the
# failure was total: GitHub refused to serve the objects, `git clone` failed
# mid-checkout, and Render could not deploy AT ALL. Not a slow build — no build.
#
#     batch response: This repository exceeded its LFS budget.
#     error: external filter 'git-lfs filter-process' failed
#
# So the tracking patterns are gone rather than merely unused. Left in place they
# are a loaded gun: committing any new .zip/.gz/.tar would silently re-enter LFS,
# hit the same exhausted budget, and take deploys down again — with an error
# message that points at git, not at this decision.
#
# If you need large files again, do NOT re-add LFS patterns here without first
# confirming the LFS budget. Keep big corpora out of the repo entirely (object
# storage, or the Hugging Face datasets the ml/ pipeline already syncs to).
* text=auto eol=lf
